{"meta": {"limit": 100, "next": null, "offset": 0, "previous": null, "total_count": 73}, "objects": [{"abstract": "   Transport Layer Security (TLS) handshakes often include fairly static\n   information, such as the server certificate and a list of trusted\n   Certification Authorities (CAs).  This information can be of\n   considerable size, particularly if the server certificate is bundled\n   with a complete certificate path (including all intermediary\n   certificates up to the trust anchor public key).\n\n   This document defines an extension that omits the exchange of already\n   available information.  The TLS client informs a server of cached\n   information, for example from a previous TLS handshake, allowing the\n   server to omit the already available information.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-cached-info/", "expires": "2012-06-28T07:00:11Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 4787, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-cached-info", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 14, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/4787/", "rev": "11", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/nomcom-chair@ietf.org/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2011-12-26T08:00:00Z", "title": "Transport Layer Security (TLS) Cached Information Extension", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Transport Layer Security (TLS) handshakes often include fairly static\n   information, such as the server certificate and a list of trusted\n   Certification Authorities (CAs).  This information can be of\n   considerable size, particularly if the server certificate is bundled\n   with a complete certificate path (including all intermediary\n   certificates up to the trust anchor public key).\n\n   This document defines an extension that omits the exchange of already\n   available information.  The TLS client informs a server of cached\n   information, for example from a previous TLS handshake, allowing the\n   server to omit the already available information.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-cached-info/", "expires": "2012-06-28T07:00:11Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 5701, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-cached-info", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 14, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/5701/", "rev": "11", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/nomcom-chair@ietf.org/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2012-06-28T07:22:57Z", "title": "Transport Layer Security (TLS) Cached Information Extension", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Transport Layer Security (TLS) handshakes often include fairly static\n   information, such as the server certificate and a list of trusted\n   Certification Authorities (CAs).  This information can be of\n   considerable size, particularly if the server certificate is bundled\n   with a complete certificate path (including all intermediary\n   certificates up to the trust anchor public key).\n\n   This document defines an extension that omits the exchange of already\n   available information.  The TLS client informs a server of cached\n   information, for example from a previous TLS handshake, allowing the\n   server to omit the already available information.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-cached-info/", "expires": "2013-01-17T17:33:30Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 7593, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-cached-