d\n   with a complete certificate chain (i.e., the certificates of\n   intermediate CAs up to the root CA).\n\n   This document defines an extension that allows a TLS client to inform\n   a server of cached information, allowing the server to omit already\n   available information.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-cached-info/", "expires": "2016-06-25T08:50:49Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 92255, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-cached-info", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 18, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/92255/", "rev": "21", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/9/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/point/"], "time": "2015-12-23T09:50:49Z", "title": "Transport Layer Security (TLS) Cached Information Extension", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Transport Layer Security (TLS) handshakes often include fairly static\n   information, such as the server certificate and a list of trusted\n   certification authorities (CAs).  This information can be of\n   considerable size, particularly if the server certificate is bundled\n   with a complete certificate chain (i.e., the certificates of\n   intermediate CAs up to the root CA).\n\n   This document defines an extension that allows a TLS client to inform\n   a server of cached information, allowing the server to omit already\n   available information.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-cached-info/", "expires": "2016-07-29T17:37:54Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 98121, "intended_std_level": "/api/v